title The line the page left out
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap in the docs-geode and prose-product lane.
rota lap 4488, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. Read the threshold, What Brix Infuse Is, The Happy Zone and the Thin Edge, Growing a Language. The threshold's own instruction shaped the whole lap: taste works only up close, so run the actual command rather than read the script that prints it, and run an idempotent one a SECOND time. Both halves paid.
think The first-hour tutorial is the page a newcomer meets and no witness runs its six steps, so the water gesture was to run every command it quotes and compare its printed output character by character.
think Steps 3 through 6 tasted clean. hello.rish printed its three lines exactly, tools/r/rish_exit_codes_witness.rish printed its GREEN line exactly, and the five-line first.rish ran under both the run and the bare invocation forms.
think Step 2 read bitter. The page quotes a three-line ending -- verified=yes, installed=0.16.0, verdict=ok -- and tools/fixtures/f/fetch_toolchain_scan.sh prints four, with staged=0.16.0 standing between the first two.
think Reading the scan would have been enough to see it, and a reading is not a proof, so the fresh path was RUN: ZIG_TOOLCHAIN_DEST=.lap/zig-pen sh tools/fixtures/f/fetch_toolchain_scan.sh downloaded the real 52.9M release into a gitignored pen, verified it against the pinned sha256, and ended verified=yes / staged=0.16.0 / installed=0.16.0 / verdict=ok. The pen was removed.
think The dropped line is the one that shows the safety. The scan's own comment names it -- the unpacked compiler is asked its version while still in a scratch directory, BEFORE the standing one is touched -- so a half-working fetch leaves the reader's toolchain where it was. The page taught check-before-trust in step 6 and had edited out the place step 2 does it.
think The second run's ending was never shown either. The prose promised that the second run rests, and a reader who takes the invitation meets already=yes / verdict=ok, a block the page does not carry.
obs A quoted output block is a claim about behavior, and nothing in this tree reads one. document_mirror_scan proves two homes identical, qa_report_card scores Truth by whether cited PATHS resolve, and a fenced block holds neither a path nor a mirror -- so this page read Truth 100 while quoting output no command produces.
obs Register held: 14 percent of 68 sentences, under the Door ceiling of 20, and the composite rose to A+ 97 with truth 100 on 17 resolving paths.
obs Against myself: I edited while the cold pass ran, so I TERMed it by the bounded form rather than let it close tree_moved=yes over a tree it never measured. There is no cold receipt this lap; the hot pass is what this lap claims on.
obs The bounded call is worth its own line. sh tools/f/fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run read 17 candidates and refused 12 by name as foreign trees and 3 as its own ancestors, leaving exactly one in this root. It also measured bakery's friction finding from a second seat: all eight ships were running a roster pass at the same moment.
loom witness=edu_tower_witness verdict=green
loom witness=edu_tower_frame_bite_witness verdict=green
loom fetch_toolchain_fresh bytes=55478392 verified=yes staged=0.16.0 installed=0.16.0 verdict=ok
loom hot_pass guards=9 red=0 tree_moved=no run_verdict=ok
loom first_hour_qa register=86 reach=100 truth=100 service=100 composite=97 letter=A+
file docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md step 2's quoted ending corrected to the four lines a real fetch prints, with one paragraph reading staged= and installed= as the check-before-replace the page already teaches, and the second run's shorter ending shown rather than only promised
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front's Petrichor block records the finding, the metal proof, and the unbuilt meter it names
scope one tutorial in my own lane, tasted command by command against what its commands actually print, and the card
status GREEN -- every command the page quotes was run on metal this lap: fetch_toolchain_scan fresh into a pen and again already-standing, zig version, hello.rish, rish_exit_codes_witness, the five-line first.rish both ways, and the recursion tutorial's three tower commands all GREEN. Hot pass after git add on nine named guards -- living_card_ascii, index_row_bound, prose_register, qa_report_card, geode_libraries, dated_spelling, unshared_citation, tracked_link, ascii_document -- all green, tree_moved=no, run_verdict=ok. tracked_link caught the new shelf while it was untracked and went green once staged, which is the guard doing exactly its job. No cold receipt: I TERMed my own cold pass after editing over it.
recommend keep-going -- the general form is unbuilt and sits in this lane: a meter that reads a fenced output block back against the command fenced above it, so a tutorial's promise about what a reader will see is checkable rather than remembered.
